::kind(api)

::meta(crate: sisho-board-health, dependencies: (sisho-board-run, sisho-board-sdk), dependents: (sisho-board, sisho-board-core, sisho-board-tui))

=[sisho-board-health]

Vault readiness, health analysis, and link integrity reporting for `sisho-board`.

==[Module health]

Vault and repository Readiness & Health (`%`) measurement engine.

Evaluates six deterministic pillars across a Tomet vault or repository:
1. @strong[Tomet Coverage]: `.tmt` source files + generated `.md` artifacts vs unmigrated `.md` files.
2. @strong[`::id` Declaration]: share of eligible `.tmt` documents declaring `::id(...)`.
3. @strong[`::kind` & Blueprint Coverage]: share of eligible `.tmt` documents declaring `::kind(...)` or `::blueprint(...)`, enriched with `tomet stats --json`.
4. @strong[Link Health]: unbroken links vs total checked links from `tomet check-links --json`.
5. @strong[Writ & Catasto Governance]: presence of `.writ.tmt`, guarded `@rule(...)` blocks, and `catasto.lock` consistency.
6. @strong[Cleanliness & Freshness]: absence of `@draft` markers and validation errors/warnings, plus documentation vs code freshness.

===[Structs]

====[struct PillarMetric]

Score and diagnostic detail for one readiness pillar.

====[struct HealthReport]

Complete Readiness & Health report for a vault or repository.

===[Functions]

====[fn status_for_percent]

Status threshold for a percentage (`100` -> `Pass`, `70..=99` -> `Warn`, `<70` -> `Fail`).

====[fn analyze]

Analyze the vault/repository at `dir`, invoking `tomet stats --json` if `tomet` is available.

====[fn analyze_with_stats]

Analyze the vault/repository at `dir` with an optional pre-fetched `tomet stats --json` payload.

==[Module links]

The link check as the board shows it: what `tomet check-links --json`
reports about the links of a vault that point at nothing.

===[Structs]

====[struct Position]

A line and a column, both counted from 1.

====[struct BrokenLink]

A link whose target does not exist.

====[struct Unreadable]

A document that could not be looked at.

====[struct Report]

What a run found.

===[Functions]

====[fn check]

Check the links under `dir` by running `tomet check-links --json`.
